# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit real values.
# Every setting, and where each one is needed, is in docs/setup.md.

# IGDB authenticates through Twitch (client-credentials flow).
# Create an app at https://dev.twitch.tv/console/apps
TWITCH_CLIENT_ID=your-twitch-client-id
TWITCH_CLIENT_SECRET=your-twitch-client-secret

# The database. Leave both out on this machine: without them Shelf uses the
# SQLite file at .data/shelf.db. On Vercel they point at Turso.
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-database.turso.io
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=your-turso-token

# Set to 1 to answer IGDB and Twitch with test doubles instead of the network, and to give
# the sample account a made-up password. The browser tests set it themselves. It is refused
# on Vercel.
# SHELF_MOCKS=1

# The daily refresh of IGDB's records (docs/setup.md, part D). Vercel sends it with its
# once-a-day call; without it the refresh cannot be started. A random value, 16 characters
# or more. Only Production needs it.
# CRON_SECRET=

# Sign-up and sign-in (docs/setup.md, part C). Accounts are made on the site itself.
# Signs sessions and assistants' tokens: a random value, 32 characters or more.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# Steam sync (docs/setup.md, part E): Shelf's Steam Web API key, from
# https://steamcommunity.com/dev/apikey. It reads the games of an account that signed in
# through Steam. Without it, Steam is offered but cannot be read.
# STEAM_API_KEY=

# Nintendo sync (docs/setup.md, part F): seals the session Nintendo's sign-in gives Shelf,
# so the database alone cannot read anyone's Nintendo account. 32 random bytes in base64
# (openssl rand -base64 32). Without it, Nintendo is offered but cannot be linked. Never
# change it once Nintendo is linked: every session would have to be made again.
# PLATFORM_TOKEN_KEY=

# Shelf for Windows' updates (docs/desktop.md, step 6): the key they are signed with, made once
# by `tauri signer generate`, and its password (none). Only `pnpm desktop:release` reads them.
# Keep a copy somewhere safe: an installed app takes only updates signed with this key.
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=
